## Prerequisites

- .NET 10 SDK
- Docker (optional, for container builds)
- AWS credentials configured (role: see vertical enrollment)

## Getting Started

```bash
dotnet restore
dotnet build
dotnet test
```

## Running Locally

Follow the [PowerShell local startup guide](DeveloperReference/LocalDevelopment.md) for the exact generated project command, Development environment, AWS profile/region, database secret/certificate settings, CORS, readiness and UI port pairing. Provisioning is an explicit opt-in. The generator's LocalMode does not apply to this API.

For an existing database, preserve the deployed migration chain and snapshot; never reset its baseline to start a fresh print. Runtime credentials and migration credentials have separate responsibilities. See the guide before applying any schema changes.

## Configuration

Configuration is loaded from `appsettings.json` and environment-specific overrides.
Secrets Manager integration is optional and must reference existing, explicitly configured secrets. Database credentials use `Forge:Database:SecretId`; the separate API-key integration uses `Forge:Secrets`. Startup does not create secrets. See the [local startup guide](DeveloperReference/LocalDevelopment.md) for environment overrides and permissions.


Ownership: Platform contains print-owned runtime code; Domains contains business modules. Data/Migrations is application-owned upgrade history and snapshot state, excluded from Platform replacement. See [the ownership and upgrade policy](DeveloperReference/Ownership.md).
